{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "38137510",
      "title": "Understanding NgRx & Its Building Blocks",
      "lectureOrder": 686,
      "videoOrder": 631,
      "sourceHash": "48e651a2e9d23e24195238e318e143cc8bd04333f60fa43001217952bb7942d1",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.13,
          "end": 5.7,
          "en": "So NgRx is a state management solution,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.7,
          "end": 9.48,
          "en": "a library that helps with managing state data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 9.48,
          "end": 10.74,
          "en": "in your application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.74,
          "end": 14.82,
          "en": "and a library that gives you a clearly defined way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.82,
          "end": 17.58,
          "en": "of managing application state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.58,
          "end": 21.54,
          "en": "And that clearly defined approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.54,
          "end": 25.32,
          "en": "all starts with creating a store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 25.32,
          "end": 30.32,
          "en": "So once you have NgRx installed into your Angular project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 30.39,
          "end": 33.15,
          "en": "something we'll do in the next lectures of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 33.15,
          "end": 37.59,
          "en": "you can, and you should, create a store, a data store,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 37.59,
          "end": 40.47,
          "en": "a state store with NgRx,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 40.47,
          "end": 43.08,
          "en": "because that is where your data will be stored",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 43.08,
          "end": 45.84,
          "en": "and managed by NgRx.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 45.84,
          "end": 47.49,
          "en": "And that's also the place",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 47.49,
          "end": 52.32,
          "en": "to which your Components can reach out to to read that data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 52.32,
          "end": 55.32,
          "en": "So if a Component needs a certain piece of state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 55.32,
          "end": 56.94,
          "en": "if it needs some data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 56.94,
          "end": 60.06,
          "en": "and if it should update when that data changes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 60.06,
          "end": 62.88,
          "en": "it can read that data from that store",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 62.88,
          "end": 65.73,
          "en": "and it can listen to data changes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 65.73,
          "end": 68.64,
          "en": "so that Angular can update the UI",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 68.64,
          "end": 72.39,
          "en": "as that data in that store changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 72.39,
          "end": 74.61,
          "en": "And for reading that data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 74.61,
          "end": 77.25,
          "en": "and extracting that data from the store,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 77.25,
          "end": 81.09,
          "en": "it can also leverage a concept called Selectors",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 81.09,
          "end": 85.62,
          "en": "which is a concept defined and introduced by NgRx.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 85.62,
          "end": 88.62,
          "en": "And it's actually a totally optional thing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 88.62,
          "end": 90.45,
          "en": "as you will learn in this section here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 90.45,
          "end": 93.33,
          "en": "And therefore, with help of this store",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 93.33,
          "end": 96.21000000000001,
          "en": "and these optional Selectors,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 96.21000000000001,
          "end": 101.21000000000001,
          "en": "Components can get that globally managed state data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 101.4,
          "end": 105.99000000000001,
          "en": "With NgRx, you have that one central store",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 105.99000000000001,
          "end": 107.97,
          "en": "in your application that in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 107.97,
          "end": 111.87,
          "en": "manages all the data used in your entire application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 111.87,
          "end": 114.63,
          "en": "and your different Components can then get",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 114.63,
          "end": 117.69,
          "en": "the data they need from that store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 117.69,
          "end": 121.71,
          "en": "But of course, getting the data is just one thing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 121.71,
          "end": 123.84,
          "en": "Components also typically need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 123.84,
          "end": 126.51,
          "en": "to change that data over time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 126.51,
          "end": 128.94,
          "en": "for example because a button was clicked",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 128.94,
          "end": 132.18,
          "en": "or a forum was submitted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 132.18,
          "end": 136.11,
          "en": "And NgRx also gives you a clearly defined,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 136.11,
          "end": 141.11,
          "en": "standardized way of performing such data changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 141.21,
          "end": 145.53,
          "en": "Because in the NgRx worlds, to change data in the Store,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 145.53,
          "end": 149.19,
          "en": "your Components must dispatch actions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 149.19,
          "end": 152.43,
          "en": "which in the end describe the changes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 152.43,
          "end": 153.93,
          "en": "that should be performed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 153.93,
          "end": 156.93,
          "en": "and add any extra data that might be needed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 156.93,
          "end": 159.6,
          "en": "to change the data in the Store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 159.6,
          "end": 163.68,
          "en": "And then those actions are picked up by so-called Reducers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 163.68,
          "end": 165.81,
          "en": "which you define as part",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 165.81,
          "end": 169.62,
          "en": "of setting up this entire state management system.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 169.62,
          "end": 171.24,
          "en": "And in those Reducers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 171.24,
          "end": 175.05,
          "en": "you then have the actual logic that gets triggered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 175.05,
          "end": 179.25,
          "en": "based on those actions to change the data in the Store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 179.25,
          "end": 182.88,
          "en": "And of course, that's all pretty theoretical right now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 182.88,
          "end": 185.7,
          "en": "we'll see all these things in action",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 185.7,
          "end": 188.64,
          "en": "over the next lectures, of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 188.64,
          "end": 192.3,
          "en": "Last but not least, there's also one other building block",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 192.3,
          "end": 195.75,
          "en": "in that NgRx world you should be aware of",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 195.75,
          "end": 198.3,
          "en": "and that would be Effects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 198.3,
          "end": 203.01,
          "en": "Effects are simply side effects, like for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 203.01,
          "end": 206.82,
          "en": "HTTP requests that should be sent to a backend,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 206.82,
          "end": 208.86,
          "en": "that should maybe also be triggered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 208.86,
          "end": 210.87,
          "en": "when certain Actions occur",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 210.87,
          "end": 212.7,
          "en": "so that an Action, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 212.7,
          "end": 217.7,
          "en": "does not just lead to data in that Store being changed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 217.74,
          "end": 221.57999999999998,
          "en": "but maybe also in addition to an HTTP request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 221.57999999999998,
          "end": 223.77,
          "en": "being sent to a backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 223.77,
          "end": 225.3,
          "en": "So that's the big picture,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 225.3,
          "end": 228.69,
          "en": "and it's probably not 100% clear yet,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 228.69,
          "end": 232.07999999999998,
          "en": "but that's exactly why we're now going to explore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 232.07999999999998,
          "end": 234.96,
          "en": "these different building blocks step by step",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 234.96,
          "end": 236.433,
          "en": "over the next lectures.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
